d at the album "IV". Asturian tonadas are a kind of traditional liric vocal songs without time. Sometimes they are accompanied by the Asturian bagpipes.N: Coyí d'un artu una flor = I took a flower from a [bramble], in Asturian languageM: 4/4L: 1/8Q: 1/4=70%%printtempo falseK: A minor % no sharps%%setfont-1 Times-Italic 16%%text $1Slow and expressive$0zE | \"Am"A3 B !slide!c2 "G"BG |  "C"E3G "Dm"F2{/GF} ED | "Am"!slide!E6 "(Esus)"zE |"Am"A2AB "(G)"dcBG |  "C"E3G "Dm"F2{/GF} "G"ED | "C"!slide!E6  "G"B/c/d |"Am(C)"e6 dc | "G(E)"B3A "Am"A3e | "Dm"d2dc dcBA | "E"^GABc B2 B/c/d |"C(Am)"e6 dc | "G(E)"B3A "Am"A3e | "Dm"d2dc dcBA |[1 "E"^G6 :|][2 "E"^GABc B2 Bc | "_(2)""Dm"d2dc dcBA | "E"^GABc B2 Bc | "_(3)""Dm"d2dc dcBA | "E"^G6 |]X:6T: The Asturian WayZ: abc-edited-by: AWC: (basic chords: AW)R: reel%M: 4/4M:C|L: 1/8K: Amix"A"ABcd eAed-|ddcA "D"d4|"G"d2 cA cA G2-|GAAG ABGE|"A"ABcd eAed-|ddcA "D"d4-|"G"daga e2 d2-| dcAG .|[1 A3 E:|2 "A"A4|||:"Em"E2 (3Bcd eA g2-|gged "A"e a3|"G"B2 (3BBB edAG|G A3 ABGE|  "Em"E2 (3Bcd eA g2-|gged  e a2 A|"A"cded- "D"dc d2-|"G"dcAG "A"A4:|X:7T: Full Rigged Ship, Da%%partsbox trueZ: MusicalbisonS: https://thesession.org/tunes/878#setting878Z: abc-edited-by: AW - Dancewiz/BREW version; chords added & revised%R: jigM: 6/8L: 1/8K: AminP:A|: "Am(A)"e2 a aea|aea "_* or ''ABA'';  8th notes"b2a|e2 ^f "G"g2 g|gag "D"^f2 d| \"Am(A)"e2 a aea|aea "_*"b2a|"G"g2 e "Em"edB|"Am(A)"A3 A3:|P:B|:"Am (F,Dm,D7)"efe edB|A2 B c3|"G"B2 G B2 G|Bcd "Em"E3| \"Am (F)"efe edB|"(Dm)"A2 B c2 d|"Em"efe dBG|"Am"A3 A3:|P:C|:"C"EFE EFE|EFE c3|"Dm"EFE E2 D|"G7"E2 F GEC| \"C"EFE EFE|EFE c2 d|"Em"efe dBG|"Am"A3 A3:|%%text (Can be played AABC for a 32-bar contra dance)X:7T: New Rigged Ship, Da%%partsbox trueZ: Musicalbison; ed. & chords by AW% new version, at Kirsten E.'s suggestion: start in major or openS: https://thesession.org/tunes/880#setting880R: reelM: C|L: 1/8K: AmixP:A|: eg|"A(5)"a2 ab ageg|a2 ab agef|"G"g2 gg 